vers every point of \\(S\\) (each point that was on a removed\nhorizontal line now lies on the corresponding sunny line \\(\\ell_i\\); all other\npoints were untouched).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.4   Completion of the proof\n\nWe have shown:\n\n* The necessary condition for the number of sunny lines is \\(0\\le k\\le n\\).\n* For every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) we have explicitly constructed\n  \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the covering requirement and containing\n  exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\nHence the set of all admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]"
